    75	## 1. The row sextic `F_j`: structure and singularities
    76	
    77	### 1.1 The family
    78	
    79	Theorem ROW-NF (charged `zvk-u6` §1.3) gives every row member in closed form:
    80	
    81	```text
    82	   D_j :  x = r(t)² ,  y = q(t) ,   r = t³+bt+c ,  q = t⁴+(2b/3)t²+(4c/3)t ,  c ≠ 0 ,
    83	```
    84	
    85	with modulus `j = b³/c² ∈ C` and the three-ordinary-node stratum
    86	`j ∉ {−27/4, −81/16}`. Everything below is stated on that stratum
    87	(the ROW-SWEEP witness `b=c=1`, `j=1`, lies in it).
    88	
    89	### 1.2 The implicit sextic
    90	
    91	Write `F_j := Res_t(x − r(t)², y − q(t)) / (leading unit) ∈ C[x,y]`, `F̄_j` its
    92	degree-6 homogenization in `P²`, `C := V(F̄_j)`, `L_∞ := {Z=0}`.
    93	
    94	*Degree 6, irreducible.* A generic line `αx+βy+γ` pulls back to a `t`-polynomial of
    95	degree `6` (the `x`-term dominates: `deg r² = 6 > 4 = deg q`), and the parametrisation is
    96	generically injective (ROW-NF: exactly three identified parameter pairs), so
    97	`t ↦ (r(t)²,q(t))` is birational onto its image and `deg C = 6`. The image of an
    98	irreducible variety is irreducible, so `F̄_j` is **irreducible and reduced**.
    99	
   100	I do **not** need the expanded coefficients of `F_j` anywhere below. Every step uses
   101	the parametrisation, which is the honest content of the resultant.
   102	
   103	### 1.3 The point at infinity (re-derived)
   104	
   105	Homogenise: `[X:Y:Z] = [r(t)² : q(t) : 1]`. With `s := 1/t`,
   106	
   107	```text
   108	   [r²:q:1] = [ s^{-6}(1+bs²+cs³)² : s^{-4}(1+(2b/3)s²+(4c/3)s³) : 1 ] .
   109	```
   110	
   111	Divide by the first entry and pass to the chart `X=1`, `(v,w) := (Y/X, Z/X)`:
   112	
   113	```text
   114	   v(s) = s²·U(s) ,  U = (1+(2b/3)s²+(4c/3)s³)(1+bs²+cs³)^{-2} = 1 − (4b/3)s² − (2c/3)s³ + … ,
   115	   w(s) = s⁶·V(s) ,  V = (1+bs²+cs³)^{-2} = 1 − 2bs² − 2cs³ + … .                       (1.1)
   116	```
   117	
   118	So `s ↦ 0` gives the single point `Q_∞ = [1:0:0]`, and:
   119	
   120	* **one place at infinity**, unibranch (it is the image of one Puiseux branch, and the
   121	  parametrisation is birational);
   122	* `mult_{Q_∞}(C) = min(ord v, ord w) = min(2,6) = **2**`;
   123	* `I(C, L_∞; Q_∞) = ord_s w(s) = **6**`. Bézout `6·1 = 6` is exhausted at `Q_∞`, so
   124	  **`C ∩ L_∞ = {Q_∞}`** and `L_∞` is the *tangent line* of the germ (contact `6 > 2`).
   125	
   126	### 1.4 The germ is `A_14` (derived, not consumed)
   127	
   128	`C` is rational (parametrised by `A¹`) of degree 6, so `Σ_P δ_P = p_a = (6−1)(6−2)/2 = 10`.
   129	The affine part carries three ordinary nodes (ROW-NF §1.3: the minus-branch system
