   131	`h(e₁)=e₁³+(4b/3)e₁−4c/3`), so `δ_aff = 3` and
   132	
   133	```text
   134	   δ_{Q_∞} = 10 − 3 = 7 .
   135	```
   136	
   137	A **unibranch germ of multiplicity 2** has semigroup `⟨2, 2k+1⟩` and `δ = k`. Hence
   138	`k = 7`, semigroup `Γ = ⟨2,15⟩`, and the germ is `A_14`. This reproduces the charged
   139	`δ_∞ = 7` and the charge's `3A_1 + A_14`, **from ROW-NF alone**.
