                                                                               TAKETO SHIRANE


                                                  Abstract. Let S and T be reduced divisors on P2 which have no common
                                                  components, and ∆ = S + 2 T. We assume deg ∆ = 6. Let π : X → P2 be a
                                                  normal triple cover with branch divisor ∆, i.e. π is ramified along S (resp. T )
                                                  with the index 2 (resp. 3). In this note, we show that X is either a P1 -bundle
