+## 5. THEOREM INF-TRIVIAL and the ZVK-U6 assembly
+
+The six-strand count is correct: (r(t)^2=x_*) has six roots on a regular vertical fibre. The *distinct discriminant-value* census in `ZVK` 227–286 is not correct on the report’s whole stratum. At (j=0), (r'=3t^2), so the purported two simple tangencies coalesce at (x=c^2); the three pair singularities coalesce to the (D_4) point over (x=c^2/9). Hence Σ(_x=\{0,c^2,c^2/9\}), not six points. More generally two node values coincide at (j=-2), and a tangency value meets a node value at
