+
+cannot vanish at a root of (r) when (c\ne0). Their limiting (y)-levels are also distinct: modulo (r), (q=(ct-bt^2)/3), and for distinct roots τ(_i,τ_j), with remaining root τ(_k),
+
+\[
+q(\tau_i)-q(\tau_j)=-\frac{(\tau_i-\tau_j)\tau_k^3}{3}\ne0.
+\]
+
+Locally (t=\tau_i\pm\sqrt{x}/r'(\tau_i)+O(x)), so a loop around (x=0) produces three simultaneous half-twists supported in disjoint discs. A geometric basis adapted to those discs makes the braid σ(_1σ_3σ_5), and its ZvK relations are exactly
+
